## Update trellis

Renovate opens a pull request when trellis tags a new version. To update by hand:

```sh
uvx copier update --defaults
```

To change an answer, keep the trellis version and pass the new value, such as
{%- if kind == 'service' %} the license:

```sh
uvx copier update --defaults --vcs-ref=:current: --data 'license=MIT OR Apache-2.0'
```
{%- else %} the platforms:

```sh
uvx copier update --defaults --vcs-ref=:current: --data 'platforms=[linux, macos]'
```
{%- endif %}

An update never touches `crates/`, `Cargo.lock`, `CHANGELOG.md` or `docs/design.md`, which are
yours after the project is generated. It is a rule change, so it can't also change code.
Copier merges the new template into your edits; resolve any conflict markers it leaves before you
commit.
{%- if kind == 'library' %} After turning on `publish_crate`, or changing a published crate's
license, copy the root `LICENSE*` files into the crate's directory and remove the old ones, in the
same pull request; `just package` fails until you do.
{%- endif %}
{%- if license == 'MIT' %}

